Subject: [PATCH] fs: File GetAvailable (0x0C01); am:net
 BeginImportTitleForOverWrite (Build 142)

Build 141 test (3 Nov, Mario Golf, eShop "Repair software"): the 0x0C01
loop stopped. The command came from the eShop ("tiger") on a file opened by
binary path (the title's content), and our "not implemented" made the check
report "this software must be repaired" with 17-1012 (FS NotImplemented).
The repair then called am:net 0x0828 BeginImportTitleForOverWrite
(unimplemented) and the eShop showed 007-9023.

- FSFile 0x0C010100 is GetAvailable (3dbrew FSFile command list): inputs u64
  offset and u64 size, output u64 available. The check walks the content in
  1 MiB steps with it. Answered with the part of the range inside the file
  (files here are never sparse); first 3 calls logged
  "GetAvailable <path>: offset=... size=... -> ...". Replaces Build 141's
  diagnostic answer (Directory keeps the "not implemented" answer + log).
- am:net 0x0828 BeginImportTitleForOverWrite: inputs media type and title
  ID; same as BeginImportTitle (ticket lookup, CIA decryption authorised)
  without the database byte. Logged "BeginImportTitleForOverWrite: title ...".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
